  "sources": [
    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "abilities",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "Passive",
          "name": "Soul Resonance",
          "desc": "Basic Attacks can connect to an enemy's soul, dealing damage continuously unless the enemy breaks free. When the connection ends, it deals a large amount of damage."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 1",
          "name": "Path of Passing",
          "desc": "Slashes open a path to the afterlife, dealing damage to enemies hit. The path accelerates when it hits walls or the Life-Death Border, then deals extra damage. By traversing on the path, he can ignore terrain and gain Movement Speed. Hitting a wall for the first time generates an afterlife bridge, and he gains Movement Speed when crossing the bridge while enemies nearby are slowed. Using this skill again causes him to enter the Seer State."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 2",
          "name": "Death's Precipice",
          "desc": "Deals damage and inflicts slow on enemies to the front, then generates a Life-Death Border which damages, slows, and marks enemies who touch it. His next Basic Attack additionally attacks up to 3 marked targets, dealing extra damage and recovering his Health."
        },
        {
          "type": "Ultimate",
          "name": "Conductor of Souls",
          "desc": "Descends from the sky, damaging and knocking back nearby enemies. Hitting an enemy hero will recover his Health and summon their spirit counterpart to assist him. Enters the Seer State after, in which his Basic Attacks will kill targets with low Health instantly."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "guide",
      "content": {
        "pros": [
          "Insane mobility through terrain",
          "Strong sustain/healing",
          "Execute potential"
        ],
        "cons": [
          "Vulnerable to hard crowd control",
          "Weak when behind early",
          "Can be kited"
        ],
        "gameplay_tips": "## Early Game\nAugran has one of the fastest jungle clear speeds in the entire game. With Skill 1 Path of Passing, he can walk through terrain and execute jungle camps with his auto attacks. With his mobility and execute, it also allows him to invade very effectively, with both execute and smite allowing him to steal enemy jungle camps away, giving him an early advantage. When looking for ganks, Augran relies on his slows and team to CC enemies so he can finish them off with his execute.\n\n## Teamfights\nIn teamfights, positioning is key. You want to be close enough so you can auto attack and execute enemies, but you also don't want to be too close that you can be burst down from the enemies' crowd control. Save your Ultimate Conductor of Soul for the right moment. You don't need to always use it at the start of a fight. Sometimes you need to save it for the heal or use it to be able to get Steer State to execute low-health enemies.\n\n## Tips & Tricks\nOnly use Skill 1 a 2nd time to enter Steer State when you can execute enemies or jungle camps\nIf you want to quickly enter Steer State to execute enemies, use your Ultimate\nCombo Skill 2 and Skill 1 to gain a burst of movement speed to catch up with enemies"
      }
    },
    {
